  "generated_text": ".. Identify the given information: $\\angle D = 25^\\circ$, $\\angle E = 90^\\circ$, and $EF = 9$.\n2. Use the tangent function to relate the sides of the triangle: $\\tan D = \\frac{DE}{EF}$.\n3. Substitute the given values into the equation: $\\tan 25^\\circ = \\frac{DE}{9}$.\n4. Solve for $DE$: $DE = 9 \\cdot \\tan 25^\\circ$.\n5. Use a calculator to find the value of $\\tan 25^\\circ$ and substitute it into the equation: $DE = 9 \\cdot 0.4663$.\n6. Calculate the value of $DE$: $DE = 4.1967$.\n7. Round $DE$ to the nearest tenth: $DE \\approx 4.2$88.",
